# Canonical Key Lifecycle example — verification-repair semantics
#
# Demonstrates:
#   - P1 Anuvrtti with live context
#   - P2 live-written lifecycle
#   - P3/P4 privileged Asiddha operations
#   - Sandhi pair marking
#   - Lopa as a hard inheritance boundary
#
# ABI word map (9 words, 36 bytes):
#   W00  0x200520F0  Ring2 Write status
#   W01  0x00AA00F0  Adhikara OPEN
#   W02  0x00CC50F0  Ring0 Store key
#   W03  0x01CC00F0  Ring0 Store inherited key target
#   W04  0x00CC70E0  Ring0 Store active, SANDHI-FIRST
#   W05  0x00CC70F0  Ring0 Store active, pair second
#   W06  0x000050F0  Ring0 Lopa key
#   W07  0x00BB00F0  Adhikara CLOSE
#   W08  0x200520F0  Ring2 Write status
#
# The historical second inherited Lopa has been removed. It attempted to inherit
# through the Lopa boundary and was also redundant: both Stores addressed the
# same key target rather than a distinct backup register.

सञ्ज्ञा स्थितिः = 0x20 ।
सञ्ज्ञा कुञ्जी  = 0x50 ।
सञ्ज्ञा सक्रियः = 0x70 ।

तन्त्रशास्त्रम् {
    स्थितिः लिखति ।

    अधिकारः {
        कुञ्जी स्थापयति ।
        स्थापयति .

        सक्रियः स्थापयति ।
        सन्धिः ।
        सक्रियः स्थापयति ।

        कुञ्जी लोपः ।
    }

    स्थितिः लिखति ।
}
